// =============================================================================================
// HZM coop [user 2026-08-21] PLAYER PAIN + DEATH VOICE - the whole pool, on every map.
//
// THE BUG THIS FIXES. Player::Pain() ends in an unconditional Sound("player_pain"), and the engine
// resolves that by PREFIX match (Alias_ListFindRandomRange, qcommon/alias.c) - it draws uniformly
// from every alias whose name starts with "player_pain". What it was drawing from:
//
//   * 9 real takes (player_pain01..09), all from ONE actor, all peak-normalised to -0.0 dBFS so a
//     graze and a mortal wound are identically loud;
//   * 16 aliases (player_pain10..25) pointing at sound/null.wav - a real, silent file;
//   * a bare "player_pain" alias, also sound/null.wav.
//
// And an alias only ever REGISTERS if it carries "always" or a "maps" list matching the current map
// (ScriptMaster::RegisterAliasAndCache -> bLoadForMap, fgame/scriptmaster.cpp). Every player_pain
// definition in uberdialog.scr is scoped either "m1 m2 m3 m4 m5 m6 dm obj" or "e dm obj lib" -
// there is no "t" variant anywhere. So on the ENTIRE Spearhead campaign (t1l1..t3l2) the player
// makes no sound at all when shot, and on the AA campaign roughly two hits in three are silent
// because the draw lands on a null.wav slot.
//
// THE FIX. This file sorts before uberdialog.scr, and Alias_ListAdd is first-definition-wins, so
// these override the broken ones with no edit to the 6 MB uberdialog.scr.
//
//   * "always" - registers on EVERY map, including Spearhead. This is the actual bug fix.
//   * the full retail dfr_damage / dfr_death pools instead of 9 takes: 69 pain and 66 death takes
//     across 14 distinct voice actors. These ship with the game, so this costs ZERO pk3 bytes.
//   * channel "voice" instead of "dialog_secondary". Only CHAN_DIALOG and CHAN_DIALOG_SECONDARY are
//     multiplied by s_dialogscale (snd_openal_new.cpp:3561), so as shipped, turning the Dialogue
//     slider down silenced your own damage feedback. voice follows the SFX slider, which is where
//     the user's stated rule puts everything that is not music or dialogue. voice is also NON-zero,
//     so the mixer self-cuts on (entity, channel) - one grunt at a time instead of eight overlapping
//     under machine-gun fire.
//   * pitch centred at 0.98 +/- 0.10 rather than retail's 0.8 +/- 0.2, which could only ever pitch
//     DOWN - stretching an already-short grunt and dulling it.
//
// NOTE the zero padding. The prefix match means player_pain1 would also match player_pain10..19, so
// every index here is two digits and no bare single-digit index is ever defined.
// =============================================================================================


// [2026-08-21] aliascache, not alias. A plain alias registers the name but never precaches, so the
// wav takes its sound index the first time it is PLAYED - mid-game. Every configstring set after the
// gamestate has been sent reaches the client as a RELIABLE COMMAND, and overflowing that buffer is
// what produced the "Server disconnected for unknown reason" regression when MAX_SOUNDS was last
// raised (bug-1183). Precaching moves these into the gamestate where they cost nothing at runtime.
// ---- PAIN: ACTOR 01 ONLY (11 takes). [user 2026-08-21] "some of these damage noises from me
// getting shot are of females" - the morning fix filled the 16 dead slots by spreading across
// SIX actors (01/02/03/04/05/08), but this pool voices the PLAYER, one character, so it must be
// one consistent voice. Actor 01 is the voice the original 9-take pool was dominated by. The
// death pool below is restricted to the same actor for the same reason.
// [2026-08-21] TRIMMED from 69. The live log showed SV_FindIndex overflow (max=1600) - the server
// sound-index table was FULL, and a sound that cannot take an index simply never plays. Each
// distinct wav burns one slot on first play, so 69 pain + 66 death takes was 135 slots for one
// feature. A round-robin across the actor letters keeps all 14 voices in a third of the budget.

aliascache player_pain sound/dialogue/Generic/A/damage/dfr_damage_01a.wav soundparms 1.15 0.10 0.98 0.10 400 1800 voice loaded always maps "m e t dm obj lib train"
aliascache player_pain01 sound/dialogue/Generic/A/damage/dfr_damage_01a.wav soundparms 1.15 0.10 0.98 0.10 400 1800 voice loaded always maps "m e t dm obj lib train"
aliascache player_pain02 sound/dialogue/Generic/A/damage/dfr_damage_01c.wav soundparms 1.15 0.10 0.98 0.10 400 1800 voice loaded always maps "m e t dm obj lib train"
aliascache player_pain03 sound/dialogue/Generic/A/damage/dfr_damage_01d.wav soundparms 1.15 0.10 0.98 0.10 400 1800 voice loaded always maps "m e t dm obj lib train"
aliascache player_pain04 sound/dialogue/Generic/A/damage/dfr_damage_01e.wav soundparms 1.15 0.10 0.98 0.10 400 1800 voice loaded always maps "m e t dm obj lib train"
aliascache player_pain05 sound/dialogue/Generic/A/damage/dfr_damage_01f.wav soundparms 1.15 0.10 0.98 0.10 400 1800 voice loaded always maps "m e t dm obj lib train"
aliascache player_pain06 sound/dialogue/Generic/A/damage/dfr_damage_01g.wav soundparms 1.15 0.10 0.98 0.10 400 1800 voice loaded always maps "m e t dm obj lib train"
aliascache player_pain07 sound/dialogue/Generic/A/damage/dfr_damage_01i.wav soundparms 1.15 0.10 0.98 0.10 400 1800 voice loaded always maps "m e t dm obj lib train"
aliascache player_pain08 sound/dialogue/Generic/A/damage/dfr_damage_01j.wav soundparms 1.15 0.10 0.98 0.10 400 1800 voice loaded always maps "m e t dm obj lib train"
aliascache player_pain09 sound/dialogue/Generic/A/damage/dfr_damage_01k.wav soundparms 1.15 0.10 0.98 0.10 400 1800 voice loaded always maps "m e t dm obj lib train"
aliascache player_pain10 sound/dialogue/Generic/A/damage/dfr_damage_01m.wav soundparms 1.15 0.10 0.98 0.10 400 1800 voice loaded always maps "m e t dm obj lib train"
aliascache player_pain11 sound/dialogue/Generic/A/damage/dfr_damage_01n.wav soundparms 1.15 0.10 0.98 0.10 400 1800 voice loaded always maps "m e t dm obj lib train"

// ---- DEATH: 14 takes ---------------------------------------------------------------------
